    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 9 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Win at least 5 tricks (out of 9) to score. Bonus points for 'Múk' (first 5 tricks) or a 'Stroke' (uninterrupted run of tricks).",
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Showing**: Partners show each other their highest-ranking card before play starts. 2. **Friðufær Check**: If a player has no cards high enough to beat an 8, they can show their hand and swap it for the 8-card stock. 3. **The Trick**: Play is clockwise. There is NO requirement to follow suit. 4. **Ties**: If two cards of equal rank are played (e.g., two Jacks), the first one played wins the trick. 5. **Leading Sevens**: You cannot lead a Seven until you have won at least one trick previously.',
      'Scoring example: Points awarded at the end of each deal. First partnership to reach a target point total (traditionally measured in stakes or 20-50 points)..',
